{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":2,"timestamp":1786504430,"nonce":"L6FoJepXi6U2VDirH2SQP6QNam8=","title":"`Service.observe` is 294 lines behind a `nolint:gocyclo`, and its per-observation decision has no seam — so the two open-episode branches have already diverged","was":"**What is wrong.** `Service.observe` spans `internal/alerts/service/lifecycle.go:147-440` — **294 lines**, 31% of a 936-line file — and it holds three distinct jobs in one body with no boundary between them. The `//nolint:gocyclo` at `:146` justifies it as *\"this IS the §B.3 table's driver; splitting it would scatter one decision across files.\"* That is a sound objection to moving the decision to another package, and no objection at all to giving it a function in the same file, which is what is missing."}]}